            "Dataset Information": {
              "Glossary/Methodology": "Data Suppression: Some data are suppressed to protect individual privacy. To prevent release of data that could be used to identify individuals, data cells are suppressed for low frequency (<5 Lyme disease records with the same combinations of certain potentially identifying variables). In these datasets, suppression includes low frequency combinations of geographic characteristics (county and state of residence), and demographic characteristics (sex and age group). Suppressed values are re-coded accordingly with “suppressed” text inserted; records with data suppression are never removed. Missing data or unknown values are indicated accordingly, so as not to be confused with intentionally suppressed data."
